{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE METHODOLOGY — /integrity · "How a winner is decided"
  Phase 9 · design/DocPage.dc.html (`doc=integrity`) · §8.20
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Rebuilt from the DC after the destroy (inventory: pages--integrity.md). Half of a pair:
  /philosophy argues, this page enforces, and each hands the reader to the other.

  ── EVERY NUMBER IS READ, NOT TYPED ─────────────────────────────────────────

  The weights, the bonus ceiling, the judge quorum, the risk bands, the community-return
  share and the people/votes split inside the community half all arrive from the route,
  which reads RuleEngine and CpiService — the objects the scorer consults. An operator can
  change any of them per programme and per cycle, and of every page on this site the
  methodology is the one that must not go on describing a system the code has stopped
  running. `default()` on a figure is a rendering guard, not a published number.

  ── AND THE RULE ITSELF IS READ ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  `rule_is_default` says whether the community basis, its scope and the judge scale in
  force are the defaults (`ideal`, edition-wide, linear). Only then does the prose state
  that arithmetic as the rule; otherwise it says an earlier basis is in force and sends
  the reader to the help article. The exchange rate — one supporter is worth about two and
  a third votes — is stated here, because "money cannot reach the people term" stopped
  being true when both terms moved onto one yardstick (CLAUDE.md; EditionScaleTest sweeps
  the retired phrasings).

  ── CITE, NO DOWNLOAD ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  This page's prose lives in this template, so there is no .txt or .md that IS this
  page; a Download that saved a different document would be filed and found out later.
  The tools are Listen and Cite, and the citation block offers Share link (the DC's).
#}
{% set colour_tier = '0' %}
{% set app_bar = {variant: 'child', title: 'Integrity Centre'|trans, sub: 'Methodology'|trans, back: '/'} %}

{% set c  = community_pct|default(45) %}
{% set j  = judge_pct|default(55) %}
{% set q  = min_judges|default(2) %}
{% set pp = people_pct|default(70) %}

{# The community-return line in the card says what is true of THIS site. #}
{% if return_off_reason|default('') == 'no_paid_voting' %}
  {% set _ret = 'Not running here'|trans %}
{% elseif return_off_reason|default('') == 'rate_zero' %}
  {% set _ret = 'Set to 0%'|trans %}
{% else %}
  {% set _ret = '%p%% after %t% votes'|trans({'%p%': return_pct|default('50'), '%t%': return_threshold|default(250)|number_format}) %}
{% endif %}

{# The two-stage editions and the withdrawal terms, built here from the figures the
   ledger and the withdrawals read (CommunityReturnMilestone::publicEditions(),
   CommunityReturnWithdrawals::terms()) — never typed. Template scope, because the
   sections list below reads them (CLAUDE.md, the Twig block-scope trap). #}
