    {p: '<strong>' ~ ('Complete judge scorecards, minimum %n%.'|trans({'%n%': q})|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('At least %n% judges must score a nominee on every criterion. A half-finished scorecard counts as nothing, not as a zero. If nobody in a category reaches this, the award isn’t given.'|trans({'%n%': q})|e)},
    {h3: 'Three rules before anything is counted'|trans|e},
    {list: [
      '<strong>' ~ ('Judges step aside.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('A judge with any link to a nominee doesn’t score them, and a judge’s own votes in a category they judge are not counted.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('The shortlist is frozen.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Once a category opens for voting, nobody can be added to it.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Unverified profiles score nothing.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('A person checks every profile before it can receive votes.'|trans|e)
    ]},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/why-the-leader-may-not-be-eligible-to-win', label: 'Why the vote leader may not be eligible'|trans},
            {href: '/help/what-happens-if-two-nominees-tie', label: 'What happens if two nominees tie'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'criteria', blocks: [
    {p: 'Each judge marks each nominee from 0 to 10 on four criteria of equal weight. Nothing is weighted in secret.'|trans|e},
    {table: {caption: 'The judging rubric'|trans, head: ['Criterion'|trans, 'Weight'|trans, 'What it asks'|trans],
      rows: [
        ['Impact'|trans, '25%', 'What is different because this person did the work?'|trans|e],
        ['Originality'|trans, '25%', 'Has something genuinely new been introduced?'|trans|e],
        ['Reach'|trans, '25%', 'Local, regional, continental, global. Reach isn’t follower count.'|trans|e],
        ['Integrity'|trans, '25%', 'Consistency of values and accountability, including when it costs them something.'|trans|e]
      ]}},
    {note: {title: '', body: ['Judges see a nominee’s file, not their votes. The votes are kept off the scoring screen so they can’t sway a mark.'|trans|e]}},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/what-the-judges-actually-score', label: 'What the judges actually score you on'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'money', blocks: [
    {p: ('Supporters can contribute in a nominee’s name, and each contribution adds votes. That helps the community part of the score (%c%%). It does nothing for the judges’ part (%j%%), and it isn’t secret: bought votes are shown as bought.'|trans({'%c%': c, '%j%': j})|e)},
    {cols: [
      {mark: 'yes', h: 'What a contribution does'|trans|e, items: [
