        ['Qualifying support'|trans, '%t% votes'|trans({'%t%': return_threshold|default(250)|number_format}), 'A nominee starts earning once they have %t% votes of support.'|trans({'%t%': return_threshold|default(250)|number_format})|e],
        ['No single pocket'|trans, return_cap_pct|default(10) ~ '%', 'One supporter counts for at most %v% of those votes, so it takes at least %n% different people.'|trans({'%v%': return_cap_votes|default(25)|number_format, '%n%': return_people|default(10)})|e],
        ['The share'|trans, return_pct|default('50') ~ '%', 'That share of each later contribution is kept for the nominee. Earlier contributions don’t count.'|trans|e]
      ]}},
    {p: 'Every entry stays on the record. A refund takes its share back, and that is recorded too. Nothing can be paid out until the edition’s results are announced. A nominee can also spend an available return on votes for anyone: those votes earn no return and don’t count towards qualifying for one.'|trans|e}
  ])|merge(_ret_editions)|merge(_ret_terms)|merge([
    {refs: [{href: '/help/the-community-return', label: 'The community return, in full'|trans}]}
  ])},
  {id: 'honest', blocks: [
    {p: 'Every free vote needs a one-time code sent to a working email address, and every attempt is given a risk score from 0 to 100 before it is counted.'|trans|e},
    {table: {caption: 'Risk bands, and what each one does'|trans, head: ['Band'|trans, 'Score'|trans, 'What happens'|trans],
      rows: [
        ['Clear'|trans, '0–' ~ fraud_monitor|default(30), 'Approved as it is cast.'|trans],
        ['Monitored'|trans, fraud_monitor|default(30) ~ '–' ~ fraud_flag|default(60), 'Counted, and watched.'|trans],
        ['Flagged'|trans, fraud_flag|default(60) ~ '–' ~ fraud_block|default(80), 'Held for a person to review.'|trans],
        ['Blocked'|trans, fraud_block|default(80) ~ '+', 'Refused before the vote exists.'|trans]
      ]}},
    {list: [
      '<strong>' ~ ('One identity, one vote,'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('per category. We keep only a scrambled form of the email address.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Disposable mail is refused'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('when a code is requested.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('A total can go down.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Fraudulent votes are removed and refunds take their votes with them.'|trans|e)
    ]},
    {note: {title: '', body: ['Being flagged isn’t an accusation. A campus network can look like a vote farm, so a flagged vote goes to a person, not the bin.'|trans|e]}},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/how-we-spot-a-vote-that-is-not-real', label: 'How we decide a vote is not real'|trans},
            {href: '/help/already-voted', label: 'It says I already voted'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'failures', blocks: [
    {list: [
      '<strong>' ~ ('The votes are still owed to you.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('If the ballot was open when you started paying, the votes are yours even if confirmation arrived late.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('If they can’t be delivered, the money goes back.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('We don’t keep money for votes we didn’t deliver.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Tell Gee your reference.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Every order has a reference starting AFG-. Gee checks it again with the payment provider and adds the votes if the money arrived.'|trans|e)
    ]},
    {note: {title: '', body: ['The same goes for our own mistakes. If our records show a voting code never reached the voter, that vote can be restored after voting closes. One person proposes it, a different person approves it, the number is limited, and it is shown on the nominee’s page.'|trans|e]}},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/paid-but-no-votes', label: 'I paid but my votes haven’t appeared'|trans},
            {href: '/help/refund-when-votes-cannot-count', label: 'When do you refund?'|trans},
            {href: '/help/votes-we-could-not-deliver', label: 'Votes that never reached you'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'sealed', blocks: [
    {p: 'Every time results are worked out they are locked: each record carries a fingerprint of itself and of the one before it. Changing an old result breaks every record after it.'|trans|e},
    {steps: [
      'The chain is re-verified automatically every day.'|trans|e,
      'A break is reported to a person, with where it happened.'|trans|e,
      'Two results can never claim the same record before them.'|trans|e,
      'An independent reviewer can redo the sums from the original data.'|trans|e
    ]},
    {p: 'A published result is the one that was announced. It is locked when it is released, and a later rule change does not rewrite it.'|trans|e},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/how-results-are-sealed', label: 'How you can tell a result was not edited'|trans},
            {href: '/help/dispute-a-result', label: 'I think a count or a ranking is wrong'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'cycle', blocks: [
    {p: 'An edition moves through six stages, always forward. Each step closes something for good.'|trans|e},
    {steps: [
      '<strong>' ~ ('Nominated.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Anyone can enter someone; entries queue for review.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Verified.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('A person checks each entry is eligible, accurate and complete.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Shortlisted.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Approved nominees go public, and the list is frozen.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Voted.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('Votes are collected, each one checked.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Judged.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('After voting closes, the judges score the shortlist without seeing the votes.'|trans|e),
      '<strong>' ~ ('Sealed.'|trans|e) ~ '</strong> ' ~ ('The results are locked, published and kept.'|trans|e)
    ]},
    {note: {title: '', body: ['Paid voting closes a few minutes before free voting, so payments in progress can finish in time. Free voting stays open until the end.'|trans|e]}},
    {refs: [{href: '/help/the-stages-of-an-award-cycle', label: 'The stages, and what freezes at each'|trans},
            {href: '/help/when-does-voting-close', label: 'When does voting close?'|trans}]}
  ]},
  {id: 'disputes', blocks: [
    {p: 'If you think a result is wrong, tell us. Every count is logged, so it can be redone and shown to you. An appeal goes to someone who wasn’t part of the first decision.'|trans|e},
    {p: ('Raise it at %m% or through %s%. We will:'|trans|e)|replace({'%m%': '<a href="mailto:integrity@afrovanguard.org.ng">integrity@afrovanguard.org.ng</a>', '%s%': '<a href="/support">' ~ ('Support and appeals'|trans|e) ~ '</a>'})},
